{"name":"Bullfighters Red","hex":"#cd4646","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bullfighters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bullfighter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bullfighters"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bullfighter","blocks":[{"text":"A bullfighter or matador is a performer in the activity of bullfighting. Torero or toureiro, both from Latin taurarius, are the Spanish and Portuguese words for bullfighter, and describe all the performers in the activity of bullfighting as practised in Spain, Portugal, Mexico, Peru, France, Colombia, Ecuador, Venezuela and other countries influenced by Portuguese and Spanish culture. The main performer and leader of the entourage in a bullfight, and who finally kills the bull, is addressed as maestro (master), or with the formal title matador de toros. The other bullfighters in the entourage are called subalternos and their suits are embroidered in silver as opposed to the matador's gold. They include the picadores, rejoneadores, and banderilleros."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Corrida%2C_Rio_Lagartos%2C_Yucatan.jpg/330px-Corrida%2C_Rio_Lagartos%2C_Yucatan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bullfighter"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg/500px-10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg/1280px-10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg/500px-10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10_-_Cristina_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/MatadorEarly20thCentury.jpg/500px-MatadorEarly20thCentury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/MatadorEarly20thCentury.jpg/500px-MatadorEarly20thCentury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early 20th-century photograph of a matador, showing traditional outfit in 1935.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatadorEarly20thCentury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/J